# Button Styling Convention

All buttons must be clearly visible with colored text on gray backgrounds and rounded borders colored to match the text.

## Roles and Colors

| Role | Text Color | Border Color | Use Case |
|------|-----------|--------------|----------|
| (default) / `primary` | Cyan (#5ECFDF) | Teal (#3A8A96) | Standard actions, navigation, choices |
| `confirm` | Green (#5ED88B) | Green (#3A8A56) | Confirm, accept, save, publish, connect success |
| `danger` | Red (#E06060) | Red (#8A3A3A) | Delete, clear, disconnect, cancel destructive |

## Rules

- All buttons have dark gray backgrounds (from the theme `bg_card_hover` / role-specific bg)
- All buttons have `border-radius: 8px` (rounded corners)
- Border color matches the accent color category
- On hover: border brightens to the text color, background slightly lighter
- NEVER use light backgrounds with dark text on buttons (unreadable in dark theme)
- NEVER override global button styles with inline `setStyleSheet` unless sizing only (font-size, padding, margin)
- Use `PrimaryButton` for standard actions (cyan)
- Use `ConfirmButton` for positive confirmations (green)
- Use `DangerButton` for destructive actions (red)
- Use plain `QPushButton` for neutral/default actions (inherits cyan from theme)

## Inline Style Exceptions

Only these properties may be set inline (everything else comes from theme):
- `font-size`
- `padding`
- `margin`
- `min-width` / `max-width` / `fixed-width`
